_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Scope this filter to WooCommerce before pruning tools.**

This callback runs on the generic `mcp_adapter_default_server_config` filter even when WooCommerce is inactive, so it no longer matches the class contract that this handler is a no-op without WooCommerce. In that state it can still strip tools from unrelated adapter configs if they are registered later in the request.


<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
 #[Filter( tag: 'mcp_adapter_default_server_config', priority: 5 )]
 public function remove_missing_mcp_adapter_default_tools( mixed $config ): mixed {
+	if ( ! self::is_woocommerce_active() ) {
+		return $config;
+	}
+
 	if ( ! is_array( $config ) || ! isset( $config['tools'] ) || ! is_array( $config['tools'] ) ) {
 		return $config;
 	}
```
</details>

