_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**A JSON reply missing `display_text` is shown to the customer as raw JSON.**

`CustomerAgentPromptComposer::compose()` instructs the model to return `{display_text, handoff}` on *every* turn, so replies are normally JSON. When a model half-complies — valid JSON but the text under a different key, or a JSON array — the guard on Line 1729 fails, `$reply` stays the raw JSON string, and that string is sanitized and surfaced verbatim as the customer-visible reply. Smaller/local models are the likely offenders.

Falling back to a generic customer-safe message when the payload decodes to an array without a usable `display_text` keeps machine noise off the customer channel.





