_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Delete the custom override during test cleanup.**

This test creates a persistent `wp_template_part` customization. The `finally` block restores the stylesheet but leaves that post in the test database. A later execution can no longer find the file-backed footer with source `theme`.

Delete the created override by `wp_id` before restoring the theme.



<details>
<summary>Proposed cleanup</summary>

```diff
 	$previous_stylesheet = get_stylesheet();
+	$custom_post_id      = 0;
 	switch_theme( 'twentytwentyfive' );
@@
 		$updated = get_block_template( $file_part->id, 'wp_template_part' );
+		$custom_post_id = (int) $updated->wp_id;
 		$this->assertSame( 'custom', $updated->source );
@@
 	} finally {
+		if ( $custom_post_id > 0 ) {
+			wp_delete_post( $custom_post_id, true );
+		}
 		switch_theme( $previous_stylesheet );
 	}
```
</details>

