_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Clear an active session that Empty Trash deletes.**

A user can open a session from Trash and then select Empty Trash. This thunk deletes that session but leaves it as the active client session. The sidebar refreshes, but the deleted transcript remains open and later actions target a deleted ID.

Capture whether the current session is in the visible Trash list before the request. Clear it after a successful deletion.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-emptySessionTrash() {
-	return async ( { dispatch } ) => {
+emptySessionTrash() {
+	return async ( { dispatch, select } ) => {
+		const currentSessionId = select.getCurrentSessionId();
+		const currentSessionWasTrashed = select
+			.getSessions()
+			.some( ( session ) => session.id === currentSessionId );
 		await apiFetch( {
 			path: '/sd-ai-agent/v1/sessions/trash',
 			method: 'DELETE',
 		} );
+		if ( currentSessionWasTrashed ) {
+			dispatch.clearCurrentSession();
+		}
 		dispatch.fetchSessions();
 	};
 },
```
